#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "PRETTY FORMATS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:13
msgid ""
"If the commit is a merge, and if the pretty-format is not `oneline`, `email` "
"or `raw`, an additional line is inserted before the `Author:` line.  This "
"line begins with \"Merge: \" and the hashes of ancestral commits are "
"printed, separated by spaces.  Note that the listed commits may not "
"necessarily be the list of the 'direct' parent commits if you have limited "
"your view of history: for example, if you are only interested in changes "
"related to a certain directory or file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:20
msgid ""
"There are several built-in formats, and you can define additional formats by "
"setting a pretty.<name> config option to either another format name, or a "
"`format:` string, as described below (see linkgit:git-config[1]). Here are "
"the details of the built-in formats:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:22
msgid "`oneline`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "<hash> <title-line>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:26
msgid "This is designed to be as compact as possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:28
msgid "`short`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:31
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"commit <hash>\n"
"Author: <author>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:33
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:41
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:51
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:63
#, no-wrap
msgid "<title-line>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:35
msgid "`medium`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:39
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"commit <hash>\n"
"Author: <author>\n"
"Date:   <author-date>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:43
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:53
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:65
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:85
msgid "<full-commit-message>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:45
msgid "`full`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:49
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"commit <hash>\n"
"Author: <author>\n"
"Commit: <committer>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:55
msgid "`fuller`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:61
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"commit <hash>\n"
"Author:     <author>\n"
"AuthorDate: <author-date>\n"
"Commit:     <committer>\n"
"CommitDate: <committer-date>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:67
msgid "`reference`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:69
#, no-wrap
msgid "<abbrev-hash> (<title-line>, <short-author-date>)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:76
msgid ""
"This format is used to refer to another commit in a commit message and is "
"the same as ++--pretty=\\'format:%C(auto)%h (%s, %ad)'++.  By default, the "
"date is formatted with `--date=short` unless another `--date` option is "
"explicitly specified.  As with any `format:` with format placeholders, its "
"output is not affected by other options like `--decorate` and "
"`--walk-reflogs`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:78
msgid "`email`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:83
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"From <hash> <date>\n"
"From: <author>\n"
"Date: <author-date>\n"
"Subject: [PATCH] <title-line>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:87
msgid "`mboxrd`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:91
msgid ""
"Like `email`, but lines in the commit message starting with \"From \" "
"(preceded by zero or more \">\") are quoted with \">\" so they aren't "
"confused as starting a new commit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:93
msgid "`raw`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:103
msgid ""
"The `raw` format shows the entire commit exactly as stored in the commit "
"object.  Notably, the hashes are displayed in full, regardless of whether "
"`--abbrev` or `--no-abbrev` are used, and 'parents' information show the "
"true parent commits, without taking grafts or history simplification into "
"account. Note that this format affects the way commits are displayed, but "
"not the way the diff is shown e.g. with `git log --raw`. To get full object "
"names in a raw diff format, use `--no-abbrev`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:105
msgid "`format:<format-string>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:110
msgid ""
"The `format:<format-string>` format allows you to specify which information "
"you want to show. It works a little bit like printf format, with the notable "
"exception that you get a newline with `%n` instead of `\\n`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:113
msgid ""
"E.g, 'format:\"The author of %h was %an, %ar%nThe title was >>%s<<%n\"' "
"would show something like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:117
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The author of fe6e0ee was Junio C Hamano, 23 hours ago\n"
"The title was >>t4119: test autocomputing -p<n> for traditional diff "
"input.<<\n"
msgstr ""

