msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:237
msgid ""
"`prefix=<value>`: Shown before the list of ref names.  Defaults to "
"\"{nbsp}++(++\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:238
msgid "`suffix=<value>`: Shown after the list of ref names.  Defaults to \"+)+\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:239
msgid "`separator=<value>`: Shown between ref names.  Defaults to \"+,+{nbsp}\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:240
msgid "`pointer=<value>`: Shown between HEAD and the branch it points to, if any."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:241
msgid "Defaults to \"{nbsp}++->++{nbsp}\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:242
msgid "`tag=<value>`: Shown before tag names. Defaults to \"`tag:`{nbsp}\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:247
msgid ""
"For example, to produce decorations with no wrapping or tag annotations, and "
"spaces as separators:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:249
msgid "++%(decorate:prefix=,suffix=,tag=,separator= )++"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:251
#, no-wrap
msgid "++%(describe++`[:<option>,...]`++)++"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:256
msgid ""
"human-readable name, like linkgit:git-describe[1]; empty string for "
"undescribable commits.  The `describe` string may be followed by a colon and "
"zero or more comma-separated options.  Descriptions can be inconsistent when "
"tags are added or removed at the same time."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:259
msgid ""
"`tags[=<bool-value>]`: Instead of only considering annotated tags, consider "
"lightweight tags as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:263
msgid ""
"`abbrev=<number>`: Instead of using the default number of hexadecimal digits "
"(which will vary according to the number of objects in the repository with a "
"default of 7) of the abbreviated object name, use <number> digits, or as "
"many digits as needed to form a unique object name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:265
msgid ""
"`match=<pattern>`: Only consider tags matching the given `glob(7)` "
"_<pattern>_, excluding the `refs/tags/` prefix."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:267
msgid ""
"`exclude=<pattern>`: Do not consider tags matching the given `glob(7)` "
"_<pattern>_, excluding the `refs/tags/` prefix."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:268
#, no-wrap
msgid "+%S+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:270
msgid ""
"ref name given on the command line by which the commit was reached (like "
"`git log --source`), only works with `git log`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:270
#, no-wrap
msgid "+%e+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:271
msgid "encoding"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:271
#, no-wrap
msgid "+%s+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:272
msgid "subject"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:272
#, no-wrap
msgid "+%f+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:273
msgid "sanitized subject line, suitable for a filename"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:273
#, no-wrap
msgid "+%b+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:274
msgid "body"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:274
#, no-wrap
msgid "+%B+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:275
msgid "raw body (unwrapped subject and body)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:276
#, no-wrap
msgid "+%N+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:277
msgid "commit notes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:278
#, no-wrap
msgid "+%GG+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:279
msgid "raw verification message from GPG for a signed commit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:279
#, no-wrap
msgid "+%G?+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:287
msgid ""
"show \"G\" for a good (valid) signature, \"B\" for a bad signature, \"U\" "
"for a good signature with unknown validity, \"X\" for a good signature that "
"has expired, \"Y\" for a good signature made by an expired key, \"R\" for a "
"good signature made by a revoked key, \"E\" if the signature cannot be "
"checked (e.g. missing key)  and \"N\" for no signature"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:287
#, no-wrap
msgid "+%GS+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:288
msgid "show the name of the signer for a signed commit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:288
#, no-wrap
msgid "+%GK+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:289
msgid "show the key used to sign a signed commit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:289
#, no-wrap
msgid "+%GF+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:290
msgid "show the fingerprint of the key used to sign a signed commit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:290
#, no-wrap
msgid "+%GP+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:292
msgid ""
"show the fingerprint of the primary key whose subkey was used to sign a "
"signed commit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:292
#, no-wrap
msgid "+%GT+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:293
msgid "show the trust level for the key used to sign a signed commit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:293
#, no-wrap
msgid "+%gD+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:298
msgid ""
"reflog selector, e.g., `refs/stash@{1}` or `refs/stash@{2 minutes ago}`; the "
"format follows the rules described for the `-g` option. The portion before "
"the `@` is the refname as given on the command line (so `git log -g "
"refs/heads/master` would yield `refs/heads/master@{0}`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:298
#, no-wrap
msgid "+%gd+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:301
msgid ""
"shortened reflog selector; same as `%gD`, but the refname portion is "
"shortened for human readability (so `refs/heads/master` becomes just "
"`master`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:301
#, no-wrap
msgid "+%gn+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:302
msgid "reflog identity name"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:302
#, no-wrap
msgid "+%gN+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:304
msgid ""
"reflog identity name (respecting .mailmap, see linkgit:git-shortlog[1] or "
"linkgit:git-blame[1])"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:304
#, no-wrap
msgid "+%ge+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:305
msgid "reflog identity email"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:305
#, no-wrap
msgid "+%gE+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:307
msgid ""
"reflog identity email (respecting .mailmap, see linkgit:git-shortlog[1] or "
"linkgit:git-blame[1])"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:307
#, no-wrap
msgid "+%gs+"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:308
msgid "reflog subject"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:308
#, no-wrap
msgid "++%(trailers++`[:<option>,...]`++)++"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:313
msgid ""
"display the trailers of the body as interpreted by "
"linkgit:git-interpret-trailers[1]. The `trailers` string may be followed by "
"a colon and zero or more comma-separated options. If any option is provided "
"multiple times, the last occurrence wins."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:322
msgid ""
"`key=<key>`: only show trailers with specified <key>. Matching is done "
"case-insensitively and trailing colon is optional. If option is given "
"multiple times trailer lines matching any of the keys are shown. This option "
"automatically enables the `only` option so that non-trailer lines in the "
"trailer block are hidden. If that is not desired it can be disabled with "
"`only=false`.  E.g., +%(trailers:key=Reviewed-by)+ shows trailer lines with "
"key `Reviewed-by`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:324
msgid ""
"`only[=<bool>]`: select whether non-trailer lines from the trailer block "
"should be included."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:331
msgid ""
"`separator=<sep>`: specify the separator inserted between trailer "
"lines. Defaults to a line feed character. The string <sep> may contain the "
"literal formatting codes described above. To use comma as separator one must "
"use `%x2C` as it would otherwise be parsed as next option. E.g., "
"+%(trailers:key=Ticket,separator=%x2C )+ shows all trailer lines whose key "
"is \"Ticket\" separated by a comma and a space."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:334
msgid ""
"`unfold[=<bool>]`: make it behave as if interpret-trailer's `--unfold` "
"option was given. E.g., +%(trailers:only,unfold=true)+ unfolds and shows all "
"trailer lines."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:335
msgid "`keyonly[=<bool>]`: only show the key part of the trailer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:336
msgid "`valueonly[=<bool>]`: only show the value part of the trailer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:339
msgid ""
"`key_value_separator=<sep>`: specify the separator inserted between the key "
"and value of each trailer. Defaults to \": \". Otherwise it shares the same "
"semantics as `separator=<sep>` above."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:346
msgid ""
"Some placeholders may depend on other options given to the revision "
"traversal engine. For example, the +%g*+ reflog options will insert an empty "
"string unless we are traversing reflog entries (e.g., by `git log -g`). The "
"+%d+ and +%D+ placeholders will use the \"short\" decoration format if "
"`--decorate` was not already provided on the command line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:351
msgid ""
"The boolean options accept an optional value `[=<bool-value>]`. The values "
"taken by `--type=bool` linkgit:git-config[1], like `yes` and `off`, are all "
"accepted.  Giving a boolean option without `=<value>` is equivalent to "
"giving it with `=true`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:355
msgid ""
"If you add a `+` (plus sign) after +%+ of a placeholder, a line-feed is "
"inserted immediately before the expansion if and only if the placeholder "
"expands to a non-empty string."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:359
msgid ""
"If you add a `-` (minus sign) after +%+ of a placeholder, all consecutive "
"line-feeds immediately preceding the expansion are deleted if and only if "
"the placeholder expands to an empty string."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:363
msgid ""
"If you add a `' '` (space) after +%+ of a placeholder, a space is inserted "
"immediately before the expansion if and only if the placeholder expands to a "
"non-empty string."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:365
msgid "`tformat:`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:373
msgid ""
"The `tformat:` format works exactly like `format:`, except that it provides "
"\"terminator\" semantics instead of \"separator\" semantics. In other words, "
"each commit has the message terminator character (usually a newline) "
"appended, rather than a separator placed between entries.  This means that "
"the final entry of a single-line format will be properly terminated with a "
"new line, just as the \"oneline\" format does.  For example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:379
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git log -2 --pretty=format:%h 4da45bef \\\n"
"  | perl -pe '$_ .= \" -- NO NEWLINE\\n\" unless /\\n/'\n"
"4da45be\n"
"7134973 -- NO NEWLINE\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:384
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git log -2 --pretty=tformat:%h 4da45bef \\\n"
"  | perl -pe '$_ .= \" -- NO NEWLINE\\n\" unless /\\n/'\n"
"4da45be\n"
"7134973\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:389
msgid ""
"In addition, any unrecognized string that has a +%+ in it is interpreted as "
"if it has `tformat:` in front of it.  For example, these two are equivalent:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/pretty-formats.adoc:393
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git log -2 --pretty=tformat:%h 4da45bef\n"
"$ git log -2 --pretty=%h 4da45bef\n"
msgstr ""
